  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Requiem of the Martyred" id="30f5-f184-7272-4778" hidden="false">
      <description>To mourn proper the fallen saint of the Covenant, We commit bravery and sacrifice in battle. If your primary army is COVENANT, you may make use of Requiem Points (RP). Requiem Points may be gained by:


- At the start of each battle round if your Overlord remains alive.


- When a COVENANT Unit/Strategian is destroyed, gain an additional Requiem Point if the destroyed Unit/Strategian had the keyword: Seraphim, Prioress, Abbess.


- When a COVENANT Unit/Strategian successfully destroys another unit.


When obtaining Requiem Points, roll a D6, the value of that roll will be the value of that Requiem Point, which may be used by certain Songs of Praise. The value of the Requiem Point&apos;s roll cannot be changed nor modified in any way, unless a rule states otherwise. Keep Requiem dice stored to the side in a place that all players may see their values.



CLAIMING A SONG OF PRAISE
You may make up to 3 songs of praise each turn, with the amount of used songs resetting on the beginning of your command phase. When using a special ability from a model or unit, that does not count towards your limit of 3 sons unless specified otherwise. Army songs may be found below.


- Substitute, after seeing the roll(s) of an Advance, Save, Damage, Advance, Charge, Hit, or Wound roll, you may substitute up to 1 value of your choice. This must be used during the command phase.


- Regenerate, choosing a unit, they regenerate D3 (RP) wounds, should this be enough to revive one or more models, then it does.


- Protect, choosing a unit, their toughness increases by 1 until your next turn. This must be used during the command phase.


- Rise, choosing a strategian or vehicle, when taking damage that would otherwise be fatal, the chosen model may instead survive with 1 wound. This may be used once per model.


- Combine, combines two requiem points, up to a value of 6. This must be used during the command phase.


- Empathize, choosing a battle shocked unit, that unit is no longer battle shocked. This must be used during the command phase.


- Embrace, choosing a unit, that unit gains the benefit of cover until your next turn. This must be used during the command phase.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
